-- title:
--   Images of the two special-fibre generic points are p-fibre-maximal
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be a prime and let $\mathfrak X$ be a term of `DRModelPackage p`, i.e. a package of data for the two-chart integral model `DRModel p` $=$ `TwoChartIntegralModel` $\mathbb Z$ of the full modular function field at the Igusa $j$-coordinate, together with its structure morphism `DRModel.toBase p` to $\operatorname{Spec}\mathbb Z$, proofs that this morphism is proper and flat and that `DRModel p` is integral and normal on affine opens, rational and geometric curve models with their place-theoretic compatibilities, the two sections `εinf`, `εzero`, a smooth locus, and the further fields of that structure. Let $O$ be a discrete valuation ring which is a domain whose maximal ideal is the ideal generated by the image of $p$, let $\kappa$ be an algebraically closed field of characteristic $p$, and let $toκ : O \to \kappa$ be a ring homomorphism (no compatibility between $toκ$ and the valuation is assumed). Write $\xi_\infty$ and $\xi_0$ for the points of $\mathfrak X_O :=$ `DRModel p` $\times_{\operatorname{Spec}\mathbb Z} \operatorname{Spec} O$ obtained by applying, to the generic point of the curve $(\mathfrak X.\mathrm{ratModel}\ \kappa).C$, the underlying map of $\mathfrak X.\mathrm{compInf}\ \kappa$ respectively $\mathfrak X.\mathrm{compZero}\ \kappa$ followed by `DRModel.baseChangeMap toκ`, the map of pullbacks induced by the identity of `DRModel p` and $\operatorname{Spec}(toκ)$. The conclusion is a conjunction of two statements, one for $\xi_\infty$ and one for $\xi_0$: for every point $y$ of `DRModel p` that does not lie in the preimage under `DRModel.toBase p` of the basic open $D(p) \subseteq \operatorname{Spec}\mathbb Z$, if $y$ specialises to the image of $\xi$ under the first projection $\mathfrak X_O \to$ `DRModel p`, then $y$ equals that image. Thus each of the two images is maximal among the points of the fibre of `DRModel p` over $(p)$, admitting no proper generisation there.
--
--   This is the statement that the two distinguished points of the special fibre of the base-changed Deligne–Rapoport model descend to generic points of components of the mod $p$ fibre of the integral model over $\mathbb Z$; in Deligne–Rapoport terms, it identifies the images of the generic points of the two Igusa components as maximal points of the $p$-fibre. It is used to show that the corresponding prime belongs to the minimal primes attached to the $\infty$-chart, in [`ModularCurve.DRModelPackage.mem_minimalPrimes_of_fst_baseChangeMap_genericPoint_eq_iotaFin`](thm.html#ModularCurve.DRModelPackage.mem_minimalPrimes_of_fst_baseChangeMap_genericPoint_eq_iotaFin).
